# Bibliography for the generated API documentation.
#
# CI passes this file to `leanprover-community/docgen-action` (see
# `.github/workflows/lean_action_ci.yml`, input `references: doc/references.bib`).
# The action copies it to the location doc-gen4 expects (`docs/references.bib` inside
# its scratch build directory) and renders it as the `references.html` page, which
# docstring citations hyperlink into.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Citing an entry from a docstring
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Write the bibkey alone in square brackets, as Mathlib does:
#
#   /-- ... following [barnes1967]. -/
#
# Any location goes *outside* the brackets, so that the bracketed token is exactly the
# key and doc-gen4 can resolve it:
#
#   ... appears in [S94], Theorem 4.3.        -- links
#   ... appears in [S94, Theorem 4.3].        -- does NOT link (key lookup fails)
#
# The module docstring's `## References` section lists each key once in full, e.g.
#
#   * [S94]: "Universal hashing and authentication codes" by Stinson, D. R.
#
# (doc-gen4 also accepts the fuller `[Author, *Title*][bibkey]` reference-link form,
# but the bare-key style above is the prevalent Mathlib convention.)
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WARNING: allowed characters in bibkeys
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Only alphanumeric characters, '-', '_' and ':' may appear in a bibkey.
# doc-gen4 does not support anything else and will **silently** error, producing an
# incomplete references page. In particular, DOI-style keys such as
# `10.1145/100216.100246` and ePrint keys such as `cryptoeprint:2015/1187` must be
# renamed (e.g. to `MansourNisanTiwari1990`, `BKST15`) before being added here.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Maintenance
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# To normalize:
#   bibtool --preserve.key.case=on --preserve.keys=on --pass.comments=on \
#     --print.use.tab=off -s -i doc/references.bib -o doc/references.bib
#
# https://www.zbmath.org/ and https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet
# (or the free tool https://mathscinet.ams.org/mrlookup) are good sources of
# complete bibtex entries for mathematics.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Entries
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


